//
// kw.cdl - the Control Description Language block set of ANSI/ASHRAE 231-2026,
// Clause 7, on hx.comps. A CDL elementary class is the hx.comps comp that
// runs it. The CdlClass instance named @cdl-<class> records which comp that
// is and what CDL calls its connectors and parameters (classes.xeto). The lib
// also holds the CDL meta, the CDL enumerations, the block base CdlBlock, the
// CdlConstants spec, the array classes as abstract specs that expand when a
// sequence is instantiated, and small composites for the classes no single
// comp runs (Nand, Nor, and the Reals and Integers pulse sources). It names
// no building ontology.
//
// blocks.xeto and classes.xeto are GENERATED from LBNL's Modelica Buildings
// Library, its reference implementation, through modelica-json. CXF carries
// no MBL version, so the version is pinned (MBL 14.0.0, commit ad48324b,
// through modelica-json 5460add3) and named in every generated header. The
// comps are hx.comps with the additions of haxall pull requests #138 to #152.
// MBL's names, descriptions and defaults are redistributed under MBL's
// license, reproduced in NOTICE.
//
// NOT hxSysOnly, deliberately: a project enables it, and 4.0.6 refuses a
// project-scope enable of an hxSysOnly lib.

pragma: Lib <
  doc: "The ANSI/ASHRAE 231-2026 Clause 7 elementary block set on hx.comps: the CDL meta, the CDL enumerations, the block base, and one CdlClass instance per class naming the comp that runs it"
  version: "0.8.0"
  depends: {
    { lib: "sys" }
    { lib: "sys.comp" }
    { lib: "hx.comps" }
  }
  publish: {"/NOTICE"}
>
